  "id": "occlusion",
  "term": "occlusion",
  "definition": "In cognition research, temporal occlusion is a way of dividing a recorded or simulated decision situation into parts so it can be paused at important moments. This lets researchers study how people make predictions, judgments, and action choices as events unfold.",
